# ATLAS was removed from Debian (testing 2024-04-28 #1070013, unstable
# 2024-11-29 #1088045).  libatlas3-base in trixie is a 15 kB transitional
# package from src:lapack that ships no shared libraries at all, so the obvious
# apt install silently yields reference BLAS under an ATLAS name.
#
# bookworm's real 3.10.3-13 does install on trixie, but only if libgfortran5 is
# present FIRST: dpkg -i does not resolve dependencies, and `apt-get -f install`
# then "repairs" the unconfigured package by unpacking trixie's dummy over it.
# The pin is what stops that, since 3.10.3-13 is a downgrade from 3.12.1-6.
#
# Rconf -ba is NOT usable: it emits --with-lapack=no, pairing ATLAS's BLAS with
# R's internal LAPACK 3.12.1, which needs dgemmtr_ that ATLAS has never had.
# So -b, with both alternatives pointed at ATLAS's own self-consistent pair.
# ATLAS's LAPACK reports 3.11.0; that is expected, not a defect.
RCC_DEBIAN_TAG="trixie"
RCC_ARCH="amd64"
RCC_SYSDEPS="libgfortran5"
RCC_SYSDEB_URLS="http://deb.debian.org/debian/pool/main/a/atlas/libatlas3-base_3.10.3-13_amd64.deb http://deb.debian.org/debian/pool/main/a/atlas/libatlas-base-dev_3.10.3-13_amd64.deb"
RCC_APT_PIN="Package: libatlas3-base libatlas-base-dev|Pin: version 3.10.3-13|Pin-Priority: 1001"
RCC_APT_HOLD="libatlas3-base libatlas-base-dev"
# Measured 2026-08-16.  src:atlas is gone from Debian, so these binaries will
# never be rebuilt -- but the pool can still be re-signed or replaced, and a
# substituted .deb here would be a silently different BLAS.
RCC_SYSDEB_SHA256="73f2db3f8bf9adf0beba174e9e3286cafca44db8dc29b8e74608b7709355f93b  2902ce22c8eae6047c937cc0b1eb5ee398a4cd79e1030b89329734175df8d1e3"
RCC_RCONF_FLAGS="-b"
RCC_LDFLAGS=""
RCC_DESC="ATLAS 3.10.3 BLAS and LAPACK 3.11.0 from bookworm binaries"
